Write next week's home workout from the current plan and this check-in. The daily tracker reads the text, so the shape below is required.

CLIENT DETAILS:
[CLIENT DETAILS]

HOW TO WRITE THE UPDATE:

1. Open with 2 to 4 sentences to the client by first name. Use one fact from the check-in. Say what stays and what changes. Do not mention a coaching week number. NEVER write "Welcome to week", "for next week", or a cross-day pointer.

2. Keep the split already on file unless this check-in asked for a different one. If the current week is full body, replace it with upper/lower or push/pull/legs. Training days per week is a hard cap. Leftover days are Rest.

3. Label every day "Day N (Weekday)" with Day 1 = Monday through Day 7 = Sunday. After the colon, use Push, Pull, Legs, Upper, Lower, or Rest. Example: "Day 2 (Tuesday): Pull". Do not put Power, Hypertrophy, or Density in the day title.
   A Push day has no row or pull-up. A Pull day has no push-up, bench press, or shoulder press. An Upper day may include both a press and a row, and no squat or lunge. A Lower or Legs day has no press or row. Do not put the same working exercise on two calendar days in a row. A core move on one day must not also be the next day's core move.

4. Use only equipment they listed, plus bodyweight. No barbell, cable, lat pulldown, Smith machine, leg press, or hack squat unless that machine is in their equipment. A band pull is a Resistance Band Row. Allowed names: Push Up, Knee Push Up, Incline Push Up, Dumbbell Bench Press, Shoulder Press, Dumbbell Row, Resistance Band Row, Pull Up, Goblet Squat, Split Squat, Lunge, Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift, Glute Bridge, Hip Thrust, Calf Raise, Biceps Curl, Triceps Pushdown, Lateral Raise, Plank, Crunch. Do not invent a move. Do not put tempo, pause, or deficit in the name.

5. Under every training day: Warm-up: then Main Workout: then Post-Workout:. Warm-up is an easy march and joint circles only. Never repeat a Main Workout exercise in the warm-up. Each exercise name once per day. A dumbbell row and a band row are the same row, so write only one. Write only one bench press. About 5 to 7 working exercises. Post-Workout is stretches only. Do not add a shared warmup after the week. The daily tracker cannot resolve cross-day references. NEVER write "same as Day 1" or "repeat Monday". Rewrite the complete exercise list under every day.

6. Write "Exercise: N sets x M reps. One short sentence in everyday words." Use a plain letter x. Never 5 or more working sets. Strong adherence: add a rep, not an extra set. Poor sleep: easier effort and "stop when you could still do 2 more clean reps." Pain: swap the painful move. Do not write RIR, RDL, hypertrophy, mesocycle, or delts.

7. One daily step line and a short sleep note. No Cardio header. No calorie targets. Close with two sentences. Never use a hyphen, en dash, or em dash.

8. If anything here conflicts with Hard Constraints, obey Hard Constraints.
